:120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nThe library README\u2019s GC metric examples still omit the newly unconditional `jvm.gc.cause` attribute.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Update GC telemetry examples to include jvm.gc.cause](#discussion_r4231716193) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5472029729","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5472029729},{"body":"[General] This makes `jvm.gc.cause` unconditional, but the current-behavior examples in `instrumentation/runtime-telemetry/library/README.md:223-253` still show every `jvm.gc.duration` point with only `jvm.gc.action` and `jvm.gc.name`. Those examples now misdescribe the emitted attribute set; update them to include representative `jvm.gc.cause` values (or explicitly state that the value varies by collection).","comment_commit_id":"1a2f1414833f6f00849539829399247e8460c2a7","comment_id":4231716193,"key":"inline:4231716193","kind":"inline","line":127,"original_commit_id":"1a2f1414833f6f00849539829399247e8460c2a7","original_line":127,"path":"instrumentation/runtime-telemetry/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/runtimetelemetry/internal/GarbageCollector.java","review_commit_id":"1a2f1414833f6f00849539829399247e8460c2a7","review_id":5472029729,"review_submitte